%随着大数据时代的来临，数据的规模越来越庞大，数据的结构也越来越复杂，如何高效地从如此海量复杂的数据中挖掘出有意义的信息是至关重要的\textsuperscript{\cite{erdinc2024mcmststream}}。聚类分析是数据挖掘领域中一个重要的研究课题，传统数据挖掘方法主要用于静态数据，而数据流的出现带来了新的挑战\textsuperscript{\cite{pardeshi2011hierarchical}}。数据流聚类（DSC）是一种能够实时处理和更新聚类结果的技术，广泛应用于点击流分析、入侵检测、社交网络、金融和物联网等领域\textsuperscript{\cite{nguyen2015survey, antonellis2009clustering}}。然而，面对智能设备和社交平台带来的海量数据，数据传输量激增\textsuperscript{\cite{oussous2018big, martin2019analysis}}，传统方法已难以满足需求。数据流聚类技术虽然可从大规模动态数据中提取信息，但仍面临聚类演化和异常检测等挑战\textsuperscript{\cite{gormus2018internet, yin2018data, hendricks2017using}}。
With the advent of the big data era, the volume of data has become increasingly enormous and its structure ever more complex, making the efficient extraction of meaningful information from such vast and intricate datasets of paramount importance\textsuperscript{\cite{erdinc2024mcmststream}}. Clustering analysis represents a significant research topic in the field of data mining; traditional data mining methods have primarily been developed for static data, whereas the emergence of data streams introduces novel challenges\textsuperscript{\cite{pardeshi2011hierarchical}}. Data stream clustering (DSC) is a technique capable of processing and updating clustering results in real time, and it has been widely applied in clickstream analysis, intrusion detection, social networks, finance, and the Internet of Things (IoT)\textsuperscript{\cite{nguyen2015survey, antonellis2009clustering}}. However, in the face of the massive influx of data generated by smart devices and social platforms, the volume of data transmission has surged, rendering traditional methods increasingly inadequate\textsuperscript{\cite{oussous2018big, martin2019analysis}}. Although DSC techniques are effective in extracting information from large-scale dynamic data, they continue to encounter challenges such as clustering evolution and anomaly detection\textsuperscript{\cite{gormus2018internet, yin2018data, hendricks2017using}}.
