\subsection{The Underlying Framework of Data Stream Clustering Algorithms}
%基于Hierarchical的数据流聚类算法将每个簇与该簇的一个代表点相关，将这个代表点通过输入数据分配到相应的簇。基于Partitioning Based的数据流聚类算法，通常使用k-means或其变体，使用类簇的中心点作为代表点来分配数据点。基本于网格的数据流聚类算法，通过单元格的密度进行聚类，将网格中心作为间接的代表点进行聚类。数据流聚类中的大部分算法都是首先确定类簇的代表点，然后对代表点进行聚类进而完成数据流聚类。基于密度的聚类算法通过构建微簇保存数据概要信息，微簇通过特征向量的形式聚类得到宏簇。
Hierarchical-based data stream clustering algorithms associate each cluster with a representative point, which is assigned to the corresponding cluster based on incoming data. Partitioning-based data stream clustering algorithms, typically employing k-means or its variants, use the cluster centroids as representative points to allocate data points. Grid-based data stream clustering algorithms perform clustering based on cell density, using the grid centers as indirect representative points for clustering. Density-based clustering algorithms preserve data summary information by constructing micro-clusters, which are grouped into macro-clusters through feature vectors.

In most data stream clustering algorithms, the representative points of clusters are first determined, and then clustering is performed on these representative points to achieve data stream clustering.  We formally define these representative points for clusters as follows:
%我们对这些代表类簇的点给出以下定义：
%我们将能够代表聚类类簇特征的数据点定义为如下：
%数据流聚类算法中，使用层次
%基于Hierarchical的数据流聚类算法：
%基于Partitioning Based的数据流聚类算法：
%基于网格的数据流聚类算法：使用网格数据结构，将工作空间划分为多个单元格，每个实例被分配到一个单元格，然后根据单元格的密度进行聚类。
%基于密度的数据流聚类算法：微簇是一组彼此非常接近的数据实例，通过特征向量来保存微簇的概要信息。然后，根据密度可达性和密度连通性的概念合并这些微簇，形成最终的簇。
%基于模型的数据流聚类算法：
%在经典的k-means算法中，原型点是每个簇的均值向量。算法通过以下步骤更新原型点：
\begin{definition}[Prototype Point (PP)]
Let \( X_1, X_2, \dots, X_K \) be clusters in a metric space with distance function \( d(\cdot,\cdot) \). For a given cluster \( X_i \) and a point \( x_{i,k} \in X_i \), we say that \( x_{i,k} \) is a \emph{Prototype Point} if for every point \( x \in X_i \) (with \( x \neq x_{i,k} \)) and for every cluster \( X_j \) with \( j \neq i \), the following inequality holds:
\begin{equation}
d(x_{i,k}, x) < \min_{y\in X_j} d(x_{i,k}, y).
\end{equation}
That is, the distance from \( x_{i,k} \) to any other point in its own cluster is no greater than the distance from \( x_{i,k} \) to the nearest point in any other cluster.
\end{definition}

It is not difficult to prove that if the data set X is ADD, the following theorem applies: 

%Theorem: 对于ADD类型的数据集X，它的类簇内的任何一个点都可以作为Prototype Point代表该类簇。
\begin{theorem} \label{the:add}

Let dataset \( X \) is ADD, and let \( X_1, X_2, \dots, X_K \) denote its clusters. Then, for any \( i \in \{1,2,\dots,K\} \) and any \( x \in X_i \), the point \( x \) can be selected as a PP representing \( X_i \), i.e.,  
\begin{equation}
\forall x \in X_i, \quad x \text{ is a PP of } X_i.
\end{equation}
\end{theorem}

%这个定理应该是一般球形数据进行静态或者动态聚类的基础。如上文所提，ADD是一个非常强的条件，我们发现将条件弱化至CD，对类簇的子集有以下的定理：
%
%定理二：若X为CD图，聚类得到X_1，X_2 … X_K，则存在X_i的子集X_i’, i=1,2,….,K，若对于X_i’ 满足cl_k(X_i’)=X_i ，则对于任意点x ∈ X，通过kTNC算法得到的聚类结果是正确的。
Theorem~\ref{the:add} serves as the foundation for both static and dynamic clustering of general spherical data. In clustering algorithms, it is common practice to select the centroid of a cluster as the Prototype Point for the robustness of the cluster. For instance, the k-means algorithm designates the centroid of each cluster as its representative Prototype Point.

As mentioned earlier, ADD is a particularly strong condition that may not always hold in real-world data stream scenarios. To address this limitation, we relax the assumption to CD, allowing for a more generalized framework. Under this relaxed condition, we establish the following theorem for subsets of clusters:

\begin{definition}[Skeleton Set (SS)] \label{def:ss}
Let \(X\) be a dataset that satisfies the CD property, and suppose \(X\) can be partitioned into \(K\) disjoint clusters \(X_1, X_2, \dots, X_K\). For each \(i \in \{1,2,\dots,K\}\), there exists a subset \(X_i' \subseteq X_i\) such that
\begin{equation}
\mathit{cl}_k(X_i') = X_i,
\end{equation}
In this case, the subset \(X_i'\) is defined as the \emph{Skeleton Set} for the cluster \(X_i\). The collection \(\{X_1', X_2', \dots, X_K'\}\) is then called the Skeleton Set of \(X\).
\end{definition}

%，对于数据集X，若它是Skeleton Set，那么它的clustering result obtained via the \( k \)-TNC algorithm is correct for any \( x \in X \).
\begin{theorem} \label{the:CD}
For a given dataset \( X \), if \( X \) constitutes a Skeleton Set, then the clustering result obtained via the \( k \)-TNC algorithm is correct for any \( x \in X \).
\end{theorem}

