\subsection{Complexity analysis}
%我们测试了高维经典数据流数据集KDD和中低维数据集breast，并使用了三种的数据结构对我们的算法进行测试。对于高维数据集，TNStream全面超越KD-AR Stream，时间效率提升最高达10倍左右。在相同规模下，MCMSTStream的耗时大约为239.51秒，而KD-TNStream则在154.64秒左右。TNStream的增长趋势均略低于MCMSTStream，表明在面对大数据量时，它们具有较平稳的性能提升。与传统的KD方法相比，BT和LSH算法在整体运行时间上均表现出更低的计算开销。BT-TNStream耗时约139.37秒左右，基于局部敏感哈希构建微簇的LSH-TNStream最终耗时仅为94.88秒左右。可见使用哈希近似搜索，确保在大数据规模下能够保持稳定且高效的性能。但相较于DenStream、DRSCDM，算法运行时间仍然有较大差距。对于中等维度数据集 breast，基于 Ball-Tree 的 TNStream 运行效率优于 MCMSTStream 和 KD-TNStream。尽管 KD-TNStream 在部分阶段运行更快，但最终聚类时间分别为 BT-TNStream 1.97s、KD-TNStream 2.54s、MCMSTStream 2.27s，BT-TNStream 相比 KD-TNStream 提速 22.4\%，相比 MCMSTStream 提速 13.2\%。Ball-Tree通过超球体划分结构，相较 KD-Tree 的轴对齐超平面划分，在中等维度数据上更高效存储近邻信息，实验结果也证明了这点。

%对于中维度数据集breast，我们发现基于Ball-Tree数据结构的TNStream最终的运行效率上优于MCMSTStream和KD-TNStream。尽管在流聚类的过程中，有一段时间，KD-TNStream的时间优于BT-TNStream，但是最终聚类总时间BT-TNStream约为1.97s，KD-TNStream约为2.54s，MCMSTStream约为2.27s，快多少百分比，说明BT数据结构的特性在中维度存储近邻信息要优于KD。


We tested our algorithm using the high-dimensional classical data stream dataset KDD and the medium-low dimensional dataset breast, employing three different data structures for evaluation. For the high-dimensional dataset, TNStream significantly outperformed KD-AR Stream, achieving up to a 10-fold improvement in time efficiency. At the same scale, MCMSTStream took approximately 239.51 seconds, while KD-TNStream completed in about 154.64 seconds. The growth trend of TNStream was slightly lower than that of MCMSTStream, indicating a more stable performance improvement when handling large data volumes. Compared to traditional KD methods, the BT and LSH algorithms demonstrated lower computational overhead in overall runtime. BT-TNStream took about 139.37 seconds, while LSH-TNStream, which constructs micro-clusters using local sensitive hashing, completed in just 94.88 seconds. This demonstrates that using hash-based approximate search ensures stable and efficient performance even with large-scale data. However, the algorithm’s runtime still lags significantly behind DenStream and DRSCDM. For the medium-dimensional dataset breast, the Ball-Tree-based TNStream outperformed both MCMSTStream and KD-TNStream in terms of running efficiency. Although KD-TNStream ran faster at certain stages, the final clustering times were as follows: BT-TNStream 1.97s, KD-TNStream 2.54s, and MCMSTStream 2.27s. BT-TNStream accelerated processing by 22.4\% compared to KD-TNStream and by 13.2\% compared to MCMSTStream. Ball-Tree's use of hyperspherical partitioning structures is more efficient in storing neighbor information for medium-dimensional data compared to the axis-aligned hyperplane partitioning of KD-Tree, which is also supported by the experimental results.

The algorithm we propose consists of several sub-algorithms. The time complexity of the TNStream algorithm is primarily determined by the DefineMC sub-algorithm. In low-dimensional cases, the time complexity of the DefineMC algorithm based on KD-Tree is \( O(n \log n + n^2 \cdot d) \). For higher-dimensional situations, we employ the DefineMC algorithm based on Ball-Tree, which has a time complexity of \( O(n \log n + n \log n \cdot d) \). In the case of approximate correctness, to efficiently process high-dimensional datasets, we use an DefineMC based on Locality-Sensitive Hashing (LSH) with a time complexity of \( O(nd + n \log n) \), which is significantly lower than the previous two micro-cluster definition approaches.

