\subsection{Memory-corruption bugs: Server crashes} \label{sec:PicoquicAppendix}
\label{appendix:memory_case_studies}

\begin{mdframed}[backgroundcolor=black!5,rightline=false,leftline=false,topline=false,bottomline=false,roundcorner=1mm,everyline=false]
We discovered \softwareBugs{} memory-corruption bugs. The inputs for reproducing each bug as well as a detailed description of each bug are available at our open-source \name{} code repository on GitHub~\textsf{\href{https://github.com/QUICTester}}~\cite{repo-inputs}. Here, in addition to Section~\ref{sec:Picoquic}, we detail three additional memory-corruption bugs that can result in DoS attacks.
