\section{Broader Impacts}
In recent years, general-purpose audio language models have become foundational for speech understanding \cite{huang2024dynamic, huang2025dynamicsuperb, yang2025towards}. However, even state‐of‐the‐art systems like GPT-4o still steer clear of deepfake detection because of safety restrictions \cite{lin2025preliminary}, underscoring their blind spots when it comes to synthetic audio threats. By contrast, SASTNet provides a targeted, interpretable framework specifically designed to trace codec‐based speech synthesis. We hope our approach sheds light on this critical problem and spurs further exploration in the field.

