(a sufficient condition for this is at least one resistive connection from any of the $n_2$ non-capacitive nodes to ground), the second row of (\ref{12}) can be solved for $\mathbf{v}_2(t)$ as follows: 
%If we enumerate these nodes last and assuming all nodes are connected to resistance, so that $\mathbf{G}$ has at least one element per line and thus is nonsingular. The nodes not connected to a capacitance form a set of algebraic variables. Then solving the second row of (\ref{12}) for $\mathbf{v}_2$ we have:
\begin{equation}\label{13}
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{v}_2(t) =\mathbf{G}_{22}^{-1}\mathbf{B}_2\mathbf{u}(t) - \mathbf{G}_{22}^{-1}\mathbf{G}_{12}^T\mathbf{v}_1(t) - \mathbf{G}_{22}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{2}\mathbf{i}(t) 
