A directed graph (digraph) is a pair $(V,E)$ with $E\subseteq V\times V$.
%; an edge exists from $a$ to $b$ if $(a,b)\in D$. 
A path (from $x_1$ to $x_k$)  
is a sequence $\pi = (x_1, \dots, x_k)$ of vertices with 
$(x_i,x_{i+1}) \in E$ for every $i \in \{1, \dots, k-1\}$. We call $\pi$ 
a cycle, if $x_1 = x_k$. A digraph without cycles is referred to as DAG (directed acyclic graph).
