A set $X \subseteq V$ of vertices is called strongly connected if for every pair $(a,b)$ of vertices in $X$, there is a path from $a$ to $b$ and from $b$ to $a$. 
If $X$ is maximal with this property, we call it a strongly connected component (SCC).

A weighted digraph is a triple $(V,E,w)$ with $(V,E)$ being a digraph and the function 
% $w\colon E\to \mathbb{R}$ 
$w\colon E\to [0,\infty)$ 
