\subsection{Establishment of the index system}
The establishment of an index system is the foundation of post-project evaluation. The index system should be composed of several independent indexes. Theoretical analysis and expert consultation are two commonly used methods to select and adjust indexes. The following principles need to be considered when constructing the index system:
\begin{enumerate}
\item Integrity. The index system should be detailed and appropriate to describe the whole picture of the project.
\item Operability. Each index should accurately establish specific content and meaning.
\item Systematicness. The index system should be hierarchical; each evaluation index should be independent yet related to each other. The index system should describe the features and states of the video surveillance system from multiple views.
\item Cost-effectiveness. The index system should evaluate the whole process of the project with relatively less time and labor costs.
\item Guidance. The purpose of the post-project evaluation is to evaluate the advantages and disadvantages and encourage the project to develop in the correct direction. This principle needs to be considered when constructing the index system.
\end{enumerate}

