\begin{restatable}{theorem}{thmLink}
\label{thm:Link}
Given a knot or link, $d,l \in \mathbb{Z}_{>0}$, with $d \geq 3$ and $l<d-2$,  then there exists an $\M \subset \mathbb{R}^d$ and a closed curve $\gamma \subset \mathbb{R}^d$ such that by identifying the ends of the $l$-vineyard of $d (x, \gamma(t))_\M$ will yield a knot or link, which contains the given knot or link as a subset, that is, it is topologically the knot or link we started our construction with after removing some spurious connected components.
\end{restatable}

It is worth emphasizing that in our constructive proof, the choice of not only $\M$ but also $\gamma$ is critical, as there are choices of $\gamma$ which yield no links in the vineyard. 
