We have the following observation. 
\begin{corollary} \label{Cor:Equivalent}
Let $B$ be $(\epsilon,R)$-embedded closed braid and suppose that $\M$ is its $(l+1)$-dimensional $\alpha$-offset, with braid angle $\theta_B$. We have that the $B$ is a circle and the manifold $\M$ is diffeomorphic to the torus $\mathbb{S}^{l+1} \times \mathbb{S}^1$. 
If $B$ is a braid with $n$ strands and let $p \in O_{\rho_{\min}, \eta, \Psi }$, then $d(\cdot ,p)|_B$ and $d(\cdot ,p)|_{\M}$ are handle equivalent to the height function of the embedding depicted in Figure \ref{fig:EquivalentEmbedding}.  
