\section{Applications and Limitations}\label{sec:bfm app limit}
BFMs are foreseen to significantly enhance humanoid robotics by providing a universal pre-trained controller capable of generalizing across diverse tasks. In this section, we explore the potential applications of BFMs in diverse industries macroscopically, such as healthcare robotics and gaming. Furthermore, we identify the key limitations of current BFMs, including the Sim2Real gap, data bottleneck, and embodiment generalization. Our analysis is inspired by the current development and applications of other foundation models, such as LLMs \cite{naveed2023comprehensive} and large vision models \cite{liu2024sora,awais2025foundation}.

