Consider using the \NSGAT with population size $N$ to optimize \omm with problem size $n$. Let $N < n + 1$ and $N_r\le N$. Let $z_1^{\min}:=\min\{f_1(x)\mid x\in R_t\}$ and $z_1^{\max}:=\max\{f_1(x)\mid x\in R_t\}$. Then $P_{t+1}$ will contain two individuals $x,y$ such that $f_1(x)=z_1^{\min}$ and $f_1(y)=z_1^{\max}$.
\end{lemma}
