\subsubsection{The Impact of $N_r$} 
From the stable \mei values reported in Table~\ref{tab:meiomm} for 20 runs and Figure~\ref{fig:meiomm} for one exemplary run, we see that $N_r=N$ achieves the best \mei value, compared with other settings of $N_r$. We also see that small values of $N_r<N$ leads to significantly better approximation quality against large values of $N_r>N$.
