\subsubsection{The Approximation Ability of the \NSGAT on \lotz}
Analogous to Table~\ref{tab:meiomm} and Figure~\ref{fig:meiomm} for the \omm problem, Table~\ref{tab:meilotz16} (20 runs) and Figure~\ref{fig:meilotz16} (one exemplary run) are for the \lotz problem. We see that $N_r=N$ is the best setting for the approximation ability of the \NSGAT on \lotz, and this best setting results in the optimal \mei value of $8$ (note that the Pareto front for the \lotz is $\{(0,n),(1,n-1),\dots, (n,0)\}$, which is the same for the \omm. Hence, the optimal \mei value is $\mei=\lceil \frac{n}{N-1} \rceil=8$ for $n=120$ and $N=16$). 


